+### Specialty directory
+
+<a id="req-vet-003"></a>
+
+**Specified by the product owner on 2026-08-08, not derived from observed behavior.**
+
+Staff read the directory the other way round too, asking which veterinarians hold a given specialty. A second page answers that, and it only reads: nothing about it manages a veterinarian or a specialty. It lists every specialty the clinic knows, by its stored name, each with the veterinarians holding it. A veterinarian is shown by first name then last name. Every specialty appears on one page, which is not divided into pages. The page lists specialties, not the full roster, so a veterinarian holding no specialty appears nowhere on it `[REQ-VET-003]`. The listing takes this page's form and no other: the clinic publishes no machine-readable specialty listing (NG-10). The page is reached by its own address alone: nothing links to it, though it carries the navigation every page carries `[REQ-SYS-001]`.
+
+**Done when:**
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given the clinic's specialties, when the specialty directory is opened, then every one of them is listed by its stored name on a single page, with no paging.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty one or more veterinarians hold, when the page is opened, then each holder appears under it as first name then last name.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a veterinarian holding no specialty, when the page is opened, then that veterinarian appears nowhere on it.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty no veterinarian holds, when the page is opened, then the specialty is still listed, with no veterinarian under it.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given unchanged records, when the page is opened twice, then the specialties, and the veterinarians under each, appear in the same order both times.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given every other page of the system, when each is rendered, then none of them links to the specialty directory.
+
+**Edge cases:**
+1. A veterinarian holding more than one specialty appears under each of them.
+2. Specialty names are shown as stored, and are not translated.
+3. With no specialty stored at all, the page renders as an empty list rather than failing.
